{
  "_meta": {
    "purpose": "M4 read-only state-question inventory — the printers/disks/versions class mapped to the ONE safe, read-only command each answers. Feeds the M4 'read-only state -> direct execution' path (auto-approvable, no confirmation) and the claim gate.",
    "invariant": "Every command here is read-only (no state change) and routes through run_command; each requires[] binary is the ground-truth on-PATH filter (same contract as the howto corpus). ships_via names the package that provides it (verified in-tree).",
    "note": "Data only. The M4 gate code (landing with M4) decides auto-approval + wires the direct-execution path; this file is the class->command map it grounds against.",
    "coverage": "13 classes carry a shipped corpus how-to; battery is teach-only (upower ships if a command form is wanted). The gpu-utilization + gpu-memory classes are Tier-3/dGPU self-knowledge — requires[nvidia-smi] gates them OFF non-NVIDIA boxes (same on-PATH ground-truth filter as the howto corpus), so a card teaching nvidia-smi never surfaces where the tool is absent. The six security-posture classes (secure-boot, encrypted-root, firewall, listening-sockets, apparmor, pending-updates) are answered by the router's direct-answer route from unprivileged readings; four read their source in code (their files under reads[], their command empty), and anything that needs root is named in probe as unread, never run."
  },
